$\begin{aligned}
& Q=c V \\
& V=\frac{Q}{c}=\frac{i t}{\left(\frac{\varepsilon_0 A}{d}\right)} \\
& d=\frac{\varepsilon_0 \pi r^2}{i}\left(\frac{v}{t}\right)
\end{aligned}$

Putting values
$\begin{aligned}
d & =\frac{9 \times 10^{-12} \times \frac{22}{7} \times(0.1)^2}{0.15} \times\left(7 \times 10^8\right) \\
& =1320 \mu \mathrm{~m}
\end{aligned}$
